<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Numantia</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Numancia</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Numantia was a Celtiberian hill town of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arevaci">Arevaci</a> near modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soria">Soria</a> in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>. It resisted Roman armies for two decades during the Celtiberian Wars until <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scipio-aemilianus">Scipio Aemilianus</a> surrounded it with siege works in 134–133 BCE; starving, its defenders surrendered or took their own lives, and the town was destroyed. Its resistance became a Spanish symbol of heroic defiance, and its ruins lie at Garray.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/numantia.jpg" alt="Numantia" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: dr_zoidberg · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Numancia_(2).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
